"e":"gev","d":"2024-04-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kenneth Parks","x":"We also continue to benefit from our announced restructuring actions, which together these more than offset inflation and higher R&D investments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2024-04-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kenneth Parks","x":"We're integrating onshore and offshore centered around three key workhorse products, which is resulting in improved quality, better availability and incremental cost savings.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2024-04-25","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"We are reaffirming the guidance provided at Investor Day in March.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2024-04-25","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kenneth Parks","x":"Turning to Slide 9, based upon our solid start to the year, we're reaffirming our guidance provided at our Investor Day last month.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q2","e":"gev","d":"2024-07-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"We began executing cost-out initiatives in the second quarter that give me increased confidence in our ability to realize G&A reductions in 2025.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q2","e":"gev","d":"2024-07-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"In addition, we continue to benefit from our previously announced restructuring actions largely at Wind and Power.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q2","e":"gev","d":"2024-07-25","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"We are raising our 2024 guidance and now expect revenue to trend towards the higher end of our $34 billion to $35 billion range largely on Electrification.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q3","e":"gev","d":"2024-10-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"On cost, we announced a planned reduction in our offshore wind headcount as part of our efforts to streamline our wind business to make it more efficient and to improve results.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q3","e":"gev","d":"2024-10-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"Positive price, productivity and cost savings in onshore are expected to partially mitigate losses in offshore.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q4","e":"gev","d":"2025-01-22","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"These agreements are tied to load growth in the US, partially driven by data center hyperscaler demand associated with AI, given our expansion plans to produce 70 to 80 heavy-duty gas turbines per year beginning in the second half of 2026, up from 48 this year, we are positioning to meet this…","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q4","e":"gev","d":"2025-01-22","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Julien Dumoulin-Smith","x":"A lot of the data centers, AI will be H-class because the end customers are underwriting a business case where they need to power 24 hours a day, 7 days a week and the efficiency is -- again, it will be a baseload H-class.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q4","e":"gev","d":"2025-01-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"I wouldn't say there's been another explicit price increase since we were together December 10th, because the reality is we had, at that point, had a very, very productive month of November and had just taken the market up another level.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q4","e":"gev","d":"2025-01-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"The timing of an inflection in North America Onshore wind orders remains uncertain, but we expect to continue creating margin in this business with our focus on our key countries, improving quality and delivering cost-out initiatives.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q4","e":"gev","d":"2025-01-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"On quality, we have lowered escapes at this facility by 25% from driving standard work and have used lean to reduce the amount of rework, generating cost savings.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2024 Q4","e":"gev","d":"2025-01-22","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"For the full year, we're reaffirming the 2025 guidance we provided at our investor update on December 10.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"While our end markets remain strong, we are not immune to the complexity at play given the current outline of tariffs and resulting inflation.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"We remain confident in our financial trajectory from here and are reaffirming our 2025 financial guidance inclusive of the $300 to $400 million of tariffs and resulting inflation that we estimate as of today, net of our mitigating actions.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"There are some places where we can pass it through under contracts that have been inflationary clauses, and we're looking actively at that right now.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"We continue to take price up, including in the last in the month of April in light of the tariff dynamic.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"Some of our G&A cost-out acceleration and supply chain actions will occur in 2025, but we expect benefits beyond this year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"We also expect the timing of cost savings to be more back-end loaded as we drive additional G&A cost transformation.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ken Parks","x":"For the full year, we're reaffirming the 2025 guidance, which includes the impact of tariffs as currently outlined and resulting inflation, which is estimated to be approximately $300 to $400 million net of mitigating actions.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"GEV 2025 Q1","e":"gev","d":"2025-04-23","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Scott Strazik","x":"We are reaffirming our 2025 guidance and are taking action to mitigate the current outline of tariffs and resulting inflation.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"}],"trends":{"theater":[[57,1,6436,0,0,0,5175,921],[58,1,7828,0,0,0,6644,836],[59,1,8317,0,0,0,7089,951],[60,1,8229,0,0,0,7354,569],[61,1,8685,0,0,0,7583,761],[62,1,8379,0,0,0,7448,590],[64,1,8169,0,0,0,